# Cub3D - 42 Project

## 🧊 Overview

**Cub3D** is a 3D graphical project from 42 programming school inspired by the classic game Wolfenstein 3D. The goal is to render a 3D view from a 2D map using the raycasting technique.

![Cub3D Screenshot](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gefaivre/42-cub3d_V2/master/images/image.png)
## 🚀 Getting Started

### Requirements

- Unix-like system (Linux)
- gcc compiler
- `make`

### Installation & Run

```bash
git clone https://github.com/gefaivre/42-cub3d_V2
cd 42-cub3d_V2
make
./cub3D maps/cub3d.cub
```
## 📁 Directory Structure

```
gefaivre-42-cub3d_v2/
├── includes/          # Header files
├── libft/             # Custom C library (libft)
├── maps/              # Map files (.cub)
├── minilibx-linux/    # MiniLibX graphical library
├── src/               # Project source code
├── textures/          # XPM texture images
├── Makefile           # Project Makefile
```

## 🛠 Features

- Raycasting engine to simulate 3D perspective
- Texture mapping (walls, floor, ceiling)
- Player movement with real-time rendering
- Map parsing from `.cub` files
- Simple error handling and validation

## 🎮 Controls

- `W`, `A`, `S`, `D` — Move forward/backward and strafe
- `←` and `→` — Rotate view
- `ESC` — Exit the game

## 🧠 Code Highlights

- `src/raycasting.c` — Core logic for the raycasting algorithm
- `src/move_and_dir.c` — Player movement and rotation
- `src/parsing.c` — Map parsing and validation
- `src/mlx_utils.c` — Wrappers around MiniLibX functions


